From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:09:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0054] drm/a9_eink: damage-limited prepare (opt-in,
 a9_eink.damage_prep)

Every a9_eink update re-conditioned the whole 1.36 Mpx canvas (for Balanced and
Smooth a serial 1-bit error diffusion), diffed it against the glass levels and
packed every pair, although drm_hwcomposer/SurfaceFlinger never deliver partial
damage (input_stats: 119/119 commits full) and a UI change touches a few tiles.

damage_prep (default 0 = the reference full pass, runtime writable): the plane
conversion records which 32x32 tiles contain a changed grey pixel
(a9e_fb_to_grey_tiles, exact), the job carries that mask, and a9e_prepare then
conditions, diffs and packs only what changed. The engine state it produces
(nlv, pairs, rect, unchanged, mask, type) and therefore every drive frame is bit
identical to the full pass: tests/damage-equiv over chained updates of real
frames, all modes, mode switches, clear, LUT changes, abort, dry-run, lost
damage. Per-pixel conditioning kinds recompute the marked tiles; the serial
diffusion is an incremental dataflow over per-pixel stored errors (a pixel's
input is a pure function of its luma and four stored neighbour errors), run for
the marked tiles and then only for pixels whose inputs changed, with a work cap
after which the rest is run plainly. Anything that breaks the premises takes the
reference pass (mode switch, clear, signature change, unknown damage, 16-level
diffusion, invalidation).

1. a9_eink_damage.c (new, pure C like the engine): tiles, converter, the
   incremental prepare. a9_eink_engine.c: three hooks gated by inc_enable and
   the a9e_end validity line; the a9t_condition call stays in the else branch.
2. a9_eink_drv.c: damage_prep parameter; plane update tracks tiles (or marks
   the next job untracked); a9_take_job hands the mask over only if complete
   (not after untracked converts, not around the test pattern); invalidate
   where old is restored (unprepare, dry run, bin refusal) and when a job is
   dropped before its prepare; eink/damage_stats (one line).
No rail, HV, gate, PG, frame-progress, fence, ring, transport or FP9929A change
(tests/mainline-a9eink-stall/damage-safety-diff.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
